Don't overlook the power of {zo'e}. {.i zo'e citka lo plise} (or,
equivalently and marginally more idiomatically, {.i citka lo plise}) is
perfectly fine, and leaves who is eating the apple as someone vague, but
either unimportant or obvious from context.


